// Phase-7 flow facet (the walk's find, 2026-08-08): a refined alias
// whose predicate carries classification vocabulary labels Secret at
// BOTH altitudes — the value's own scheme, and a source FN's flow
// character (the TFun arm joins the RETURN's label with the row's;
// pre-fix it read the row alone, so `flow getpw` on a `-> Vault`
// source answered Public). The type name avoids `Secret`/`Public` —
// FlowLabel's own constructors occupy the user namespace.
type Vault = String where classified(self)

fn classified(s: String) -> Bool = true
let pw: Vault = "hunter2"
fn getpw() -> Vault = "hunter2"
fn main() = 0
